Challenge to take on 
 We are looking for someone to define and support the implementation of cloud and hybrid solution architectures that meet business needs and security, performance, availability, and operational requirements. They will contribute to modernizing existing products, new projects, and reusing LGI's shared capabilities.
 As a cross-functional specialist, the person will work with application solution architects, internal teams, clients, and partners to transform architectural directions into feasible solutions. Application architects remain responsible for the overall architecture of their products and solutions.
 Main responsibilities 
 The person will notably have:
 • Collaborate with application architects on the design of cloud and hybrid components of solutions, including hosting, services, networks, connectivity, and flows between environments;
 • Support product modernization and assess possible paths: maintaining hybrid environments, moving components, gradual overhaul, or adoption of cloud services;
 • Support clients and teams in solution migration and STI consolidation, including a lift and shift approach, by assessing dependencies, latency, capacity, prerequisites, and risks;
 • Adapt solutions to the requirements of Santé Québec and institutions regarding hosting, data residency, security, availability, and operational responsibility sharing;
 • Collaborate with CloudOps, SRE, infrastructure and security teams to integrate deployment, monitoring, backups, recovery, and support from the design stage;
 • Compare options according to their costs, risks, and impacts on performance, availability, security, and operations; contribute to sizing and cost estimates;
 • Contribute to reusable guidelines and patterns, including hosting, identity, logging, and deployment;
 • Document choices, trade-offs, dependencies, and risks for projects and RMP/SDLC governance stages;
 • Participate in setting expectations for partners, review their proposals and deliverables, and facilitate knowledge transfer to LGI teams.
Qualifications 
 Essential skills and experiences 
 • Experience in cloud solution architecture, mainly on Microsoft Azure, and in hybrid environments;
 • Experience with private hosting, including VMware virtualized infrastructures, as well as a good knowledge of virtual desktops and application publishing;
 • Experience in designing hosting solutions and migrating application loads, including dependency and risk analysis;
 • Good understanding of infrastructure, networks, connectivity, and latency issues;
 • Good knowledge of Azure application services, virtual machines, containers, and managed services;
 • Ability to integrate security, monitoring, backup, recovery, and deployment needs into the design;
 • Ability to evaluate options according to technical requirements, costs, risks, and operational constraints;
 • Experience collaborating with application architects and development, infrastructure, security, and operations teams;
 • Ability to popularize technical options, document decisions, and formulate recommendations tailored to project constraints.
 Expected deliverables 
 In collaboration with relevant teams, help document cloud and hybrid architectures, options and recommendations, technical requirements, migration analyses, capacity and cost assumptions, as well as operational needs and responsibilities. Record decisions, risks, and dependencies, and contribute to reusable guidance and the review of partner deliverables.
 Project examples and contexts 
 The person will be able to work on consolidating ITCs, hosting within Santé Québec's tenant, provincial-level solutions, modernizing legacy applications, containerized applications, as well as projects related to data, integrations, and identity.
Why join LGI? 
 A workplace built on trust, autonomy and collaboration 
 The opportunity to grow, perform and work alongside curious and talented colleagues 
 A continuous learning culture with dedicated training time, a renowed skills development platform and access to cutting-edge tools 
 Stimulating projects that advance healthcare technology and support the work of over 320,000 professionals, benefiting more than 6 million patients 
 A comprehensive benefits package including group insurance from day one, a group RRSP with employer contributions, 24/7 telemedicine, an employee and family assistance program, and a minimum of 3 weeks vacation per year 
